            <div xml:id="d458-a1">

                <pb facs="0456" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg432"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Bargash to Mr.
                        McMath.</head>
                <p>Praise be to the one God!</p>
                <p>To our beloved and wise friend Jesse H. McMath, esq., United States consul
                    general: We are always making inquiry regarding your welfare and praying God you
                    are well.</p>
                <p>I have to inform you that our master the Sultan, protected by God, has acceded in
                    planning free commerce in conformity with treaty stipulations, and it is my duty
                    to inform you thereof; and peace !</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">On <date calendar="hijri gregorian"
                            when="1864-06-12">9th Muharram, year 1281, equal to 12th June,
                            1864</date>.</dateline><lb/>The employé of the elevated throne, <lb/>
                    <signed>MOHAMED BARGASH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
